<article class="env-definition" id="01IJ">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01IJ">Definition <span data-tag="01IJ">26.9.1</span>.</a> A <em>scheme</em> is a locally ringed space with the property that every point has an open neighbourhood which is an affine scheme. A <em>morphism of schemes</em> is a morphism of locally ringed spaces. The category of schemes will be denoted $\mathit{Sch}$. </p>
